{"id": "EUVD-2026-103875", "enisaUuid": "52bcf58e-0c81-371d-83be-42fa333bdecc", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nperf: Fix race between perf_event_exit_task() and perf_pending_task()\n\nA race condition exists between perf_event_exit_task() and\nperf_pending_task() during begin_new_exec().\n\nDuring begin_new_exec(), perf_event_exit_task() may be called, and the\nPF_EXITING flag is not set on task. So perf_sigtrap() continues to execute\nand triggers WARN_ON_ONCE(event->ctx->task != current).\n\nSince both task exit and exec paths can call perf_event_exit_task() which\nsets ctx->task to TASK_TOMBSTONE, fix this by explicitly checking if\nevent->ctx->task equals TASK_TOMBSTONE and dropping the redundant\nPF_EXITING check.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:48:27", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:57:00", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/655acfa713bce9ae9c81a654459890c2f58cb4e8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/672b8a9ce8f51b991481dfde26fba5cc4340a91a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/524063fea29f8a841e49927ea7a8085194ad3ec2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/81e61e3f8befa1bae3ec8e779d8ada5e5e362c21", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ffb684f2aa141eeb0caa6308422e7e05d1ded7c4"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98790", "GHSA-hx5j-phv4-m97w"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0b8b558d-d4a0-33e4-92b4-397e22b80c7d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "97ba62b278674293762c3d91f724f1bb922f04e0 <524063fea29f8a841e49927ea7a8085194ad3ec2"}, {"id": "19b64041-a338-339c-b45f-8af0a00b9aa8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "40fc2032-dd89-3867-b7b7-36678e59baa4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "459cd8a4-0d39-3a8e-a741-3c5e50f98b6b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "5d0e849d-8918-32f9-95d6-469808132bbc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "620039ce-3bb6-3232-bcc9-ae5c1b7a38d0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "97ba62b278674293762c3d91f724f1bb922f04e0 <655acfa713bce9ae9c81a654459890c2f58cb4e8"}, {"id": "67561687-9c3d-3b1e-aedf-4e9a48493135", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "97ba62b278674293762c3d91f724f1bb922f04e0 <ffb684f2aa141eeb0caa6308422e7e05d1ded7c4"}, {"id": "767698cf-538b-38f6-bf30-7418bc3a57bc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.13"}, {"id": "82a92bb0-043a-39ee-904d-f27571e924d5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "97ba62b278674293762c3d91f724f1bb922f04e0 <672b8a9ce8f51b991481dfde26fba5cc4340a91a"}, {"id": "947f66fe-cc5d-3f03-9889-3b803494dd67", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "97ba62b278674293762c3d91f724f1bb922f04e0 <81e61e3f8befa1bae3ec8e779d8ada5e5e362c21"}, {"id": "d46c2c58-ea84-335a-9906-7ef984169643", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "e1addf6e-6826-3834-a03d-203dd736c20d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "a55be2c0-b0e3-3909-9106-be4ebd90a1be", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}